## ⏯️ ON BOOT (whole project)
You are `unify` — you actively CONNECT the domains and steward the overall. **Boot live in
ONE command:** `chrysalis coord set unify task='booting'` (creates/owns `coord/unify.ys` +
joins the board through the gated codec — NEVER hand-edit a heartbeat; ROSTER §How it works).
Then read this, `coord/ROSTER.md`, `docs/grand-synthesis.md`, `docs/categorical-core.md`,
`docs/NEXT-SESSION.md`. Own `coord/unify.ys` (live) and this file (durable). Then read
each agent's `coord/<agent>.next` for their detail. This file is the navigational
overall; the deep docs hold the content.

## The convergence map (why this is ONE project)
- **One engine.** biology / quantum / synthesis are the SAME machine — prism's BRS +
  the closed schema algebra + the mesh — over `node · link · couple · split ·
  distribute · generate`. Each domain instantiates the columns; nothing is bespoke.
- **The categorical spine** (`categorical-core.md`): domains = presented symmetric
  monoidal theories (props/Lawvere); couplings & protocols = functors; `fold`/`unfurl`
  = cup/cap = entanglement = M/R-closure = reflection.
- **Three convergences, one idea:** confluence (rewrite) · CRDT (replicas) · dynamical
  attractor (phase-lock) — Demo 2 STACKED the last two over a socket.
- **The CALM axis** (monotone ⟺ coordination-free) governs BOTH the substrate (mesh)
  AND our own workflow (per-source files vs the shared build invariant). See ROSTER.

